{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T07:07:44.829Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-12T07:07:44.828Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"PR 1711 Codex review round 2, fixed in this PR. (P2) Filtering notice-mode failures to expired, invalid_registry and invalid_waiver still let a malformed explicit waiver (invalid_gate_evidence), a producer-less boundary (invalid_boundary) or a skipped duplicate (duplicate_boundary) hide an expiry, so the warning passed with no notices. Notice mode now fails on every boundary or defect-evidence finding plus every notice; only recurrence-policy findings stay out. The spec covers all four record shapes. (P3, on pm-pvun8c's check) isPackagedPath used path.posix.matchesGlob, which skips dot-prefixed segments, while npm's packlist includes them, so plugins/pm-codex/.mcp.json under plugins/** read as unshipped. Leading-dot segments are now neutralized in both path and pattern before matching; the spec covers dot files and directories under a wildcard and an explicit dot pattern.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T07:07:44.829Z"}],"before_hash":"7e2ee008f351c17a59a2af1b113a320947fec6bccfdc2b163a34fc6dd1c4b3e2","after_hash":"ab1ed64e92e56cbcf781d2bd6d4760c6226f0d20a93ecb45058fb1eaf6ccaa8e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive",